Maktaba shared test fixtures — licensing
========================================

Story 20.2 AC4 requires an explicit licence statement covering every
committed sample. This file is the single source of that statement.

1. Synthetic / structural fixtures (committed today)
   ---------------------------------------------------
   Every file currently committed under shared/fixtures/ is either:

     * hand-authored JSON (the probe-goldens/*.json edge-case
       descriptors), or
     * documentation / manifests (README.md, *.manifest.json).

   These contain NO third-party media and NO copyrighted content.
   They are original work, released under the same licence as the
   Maktaba repository (see the repository-root LICENSE). They may be
   freely used, modified, and redistributed within this project.

2. Real media samples (NOT yet committed — see README.md "DEFERRED")
   -----------------------------------------------------------------
   The Story 20.2 AC1 audio/video samples (Arabic / English / mixed /
   multitrack / 4K-HDR) are deliberately NOT committed yet. When they
   are introduced, EACH sample MUST arrive with its own provenance and
   licence recorded in this file, one stanza per sample, e.g.:

     samples/<name>.<ext>
       source:   <url or "self-recorded">
       licence:  <CC0 / CC-BY-4.0 / public-domain / self, all-rights>
       sha256:   <hash, must match samples/<name>.sha256>

   A sample with no stanza here is a Story 20.2 AC4 violation and the
   fixtures-check gate (when it lands) must reject it. Until then this
   section is intentionally empty: there are no media samples to cover.
